{
  "info": {
    "name": "Chat App REST — Complete REST Flow",
    "description": "Run requests 01–21 manually in order. Before each dependent request, copy IDs and tokens from the previous response into the collection variables; this collection intentionally contains no scripts that generate or overwrite variable data. Set emailA, emailB, and password before registration. Password must contain 8+ Unicode code points and at most 72 UTF-8 bytes. Requires the API on baseUrl with current migrations applied. The requests cover registration, login, access/refresh tokens, user discovery, direct chat, messaging, unread/read state, conversation reuse, private/public profiles, profile updates, the three HTTP 401 error codes, and browser WebSocket ticket issuance. Set webOrigin to an exact configured origin; copy data.ticket from request 21 into /ws?ticket=... with matching Origin and no Authorization. Fresh ticket per attempt. Import docs/chat-app-websocket.asyncapi.json separately for the bidirectional WebSocket protocol; Postman does not mix HTTP and WebSocket requests in one multi-protocol collection.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
